      "knowledge_point": "Perpendicular Vectors",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨0,1,-5⟩$ and $b=⟨6,x,-2⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6+1\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =x+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x+10 & =0 \\\\ x & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
